  "term": "flurazepam",
  "definition": "Flurazepam is a benzodiazepine drug that depresses central nervous system activity and has sedative and sleep-inducing effects. It works by enhancing the action of GABA-A receptors, which reduces neuronal excitability and helps suppress arousal in the brain.",
